URGENT BUG FIX: WhatsApp-style Swipe-to-Reply is not working in Joy Inbox.

The quoted reply feature was implemented, but swiping a chat message does nothing.

Please inspect the existing code and fix the actual swipe interaction.

Requirements:

1. Allow users to swipe an individual message to the right to trigger Reply.
2. Show a smooth WhatsApp-style swipe animation.
3. Display a reply icon while swiping.
4. When the swipe threshold is reached, activate the existing quoted-reply functionality.
5. Show the selected original message preview above the message composer.
6. Sending the reply must correctly reference the original WhatsApp message ID.
7. Support both incoming customer messages and outgoing messages.
8. Support touch gestures on Android/mobile and mouse or trackpad interactions on desktop.
9. Prevent normal vertical scrolling from accidentally triggering reply.
10. Ensure swipe gestures do not interfere with message selection, scrolling, or existing chat actions.

IMPORTANT:

- First inspect the existing implementation and identify why swipe-to-reply is not working.
- Reuse the existing quoted-reply functionality. Do not create a separate fake reply system.
- Do not rebuild Joy Inbox.
- Do not break Firebase synchronization, WhatsApp Cloud API, chat history, or notifications.
- Preserve the existing UI and design.
- Test the feature after implementation.

After fixing:

- Run the frontend production build.
- Check for TypeScript and runtime errors.
- List the exact files changed.
- Explain the actual cause of the bug.
- Do not claim it is fixed unless the implementation and build have been verified.

